WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Tesla is updating its Canadian Model 3 page with Fremont Long Range RWD specs after Shanghai

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:12.080
units hit quota limits. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 647. The inverter headed for Model

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:18.780
3 lines, Houston's Robotaxi map, and Latvia on fsd follow from there. Electric reports the

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:26.800
premium rear-wheel drive page now lists 584 km of range, and a 5.2 second run from 0-100 km

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.040
per hour. That range in Sprint matched the Fremont Long Range rear-wheel drive car Canada

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:38.320
sold two years ago. The Shanghai car that used to sit on that page at $39,490 Canadian

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:45.280
dollars was listed at 463 kilometers and 6.2 seconds. The listing now shows a curb weight

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:52.680
of 1,745 kilograms. A change Canadian owners first spotted on X. Shanghai built orders

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:59.180
state paused, pending a new government quota expected in March 2027, and Canada's 25%

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.160
counter tariffs on U.S. made vehicles are still in force.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.740
The U.S. site rates the same Fremont car at 363 miles of EPA range, and 0-60 miles per

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:18.120
hour in 4.9 seconds, starting at $42,490, which is the Model 3 premium rear-wheel drive Tesla

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.340
cells in the U.S. today.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.520
Tesla's Canadian comparison page still shows the older Shanghai figures, and in

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:30.980
October 2024, the Fremont Long Range rear-wheel drive qualified for the Federal IZE rebate

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.140
at a $54,990 starting price.

00:01:35.126 --> 00:01:40.266
Head of Drive Unit Engineering, Nick Verzini said the new inverter board uses far fewer electronic

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.966
components and supports multiple suppliers.

00:01:43.506 --> 00:01:47.446
Tesla Roddy reports the board drops straight into a model-wide drive unit.

00:01:47.446 --> 00:01:51.886
Verzini confirmed the printed circuit board assembly and power stage will reach

00:01:51.886 --> 00:01:57.406
Model 3 lines before year end. The design keeps the entire interface compatible with existing

00:01:57.406 --> 00:02:03.586
drive unit architecture. The CyberCab drive unit also runs an 11-to-1 gear ratio instead of

00:02:03.586 --> 00:02:09.086
the roughly 9-to-1 ratio used on most current Teslas. The same components were developed to

00:02:09.086 --> 00:02:15.182
reduce supplier risk and simplify assembly across platforms. Houston's Robotaxi Zone grew

00:02:15.182 --> 00:02:19.622
from 25 to 254 square miles, digital today reports.

00:02:20.182 --> 00:02:22.842
The new area covers 1.3 million residents.

00:02:23.302 --> 00:02:26.022
The active fleet currently stands at 34 vehicles.

00:02:26.522 --> 00:02:31.142
The geofence now reaches roughly five times the size of Waymo's operating area in the

00:02:31.142 --> 00:02:31.762
same city.

00:02:32.262 --> 00:02:34.962
The shape of the new boundary resembles a rocket silhouette.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:39.982
Service remains limited to that small active fleet despite the larger map territory.

00:02:39.982 --> 00:02:46.712
FSD supervised is now approved for public roads in Latvia, according to NOT a Tesla app.

00:02:47.152 --> 00:02:53.132
Rollout begins soon and starts with HW-4 vehicles running the European build of FSD-V14.

00:02:53.852 --> 00:02:59.312
Latvia joins Lithuania and Estonia as the 10th EU member to approve the system independently.

00:02:59.772 --> 00:03:02.812
And FSD is now approved in 18 countries worldwide.

00:03:03.432 --> 00:03:08.312
The EU wide vote is scheduled for December, and Germany has indicated it will support the

00:03:08.312 --> 00:03:11.712
measure if speed offset stays within 10% of posted limits.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:16.672
Slovakia became the ninth country to approve the software less than two weeks earlier.

00:03:17.212 --> 00:03:21.352
The Baltic approvals now form a contiguous regional block for early deployment.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:27.075
Turo hosts can now link their Tesla account to confirm which cars have FSD supervised.

00:03:27.775 --> 00:03:33.455
Inside EVs reports that Tesla models that qualify for FSD but lack it installed become eligible

00:03:33.455 --> 00:03:35.095
for a one-month free trial.

00:03:35.095 --> 00:03:38.875
The revised interface launches October 28th.

00:03:38.915 --> 00:03:42.935
Renters receive a Turo disclaimer that they must supervise the vehicle at all times.

00:03:43.575 --> 00:03:48.955
Turo says Tesla Model 3 and Model Y already rank as its third and fourth most rented cars.

00:03:49.655 --> 00:03:55.075
Hosts share data directly so Turo can verify FSD status without relying on owner descriptions

00:03:55.605 --> 00:03:59.875
and hosts who add FSD through the trial can offer the feature to renters immediately.

00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:06.172
Heavy-duty charging for the Tesla semi is live at the first two pilot locations, transport

00:04:06.172 --> 00:04:11.532
topics reports. Those stops mark the initial rollout of Tesla's semi-compatible chargers

00:04:11.532 --> 00:04:17.372
at pilot facilities. Both sites are now operational for commercial electric trucks. The partnership

00:04:17.372 --> 00:04:23.719
focuses on high-power charging corridors for long-haul routes. Fort Bend County offered a 30-year

00:04:23.719 --> 00:04:29.679
incentives package to attract Tesla's proposed $10 billion solar panel facility. Yahoo Finance

00:04:29.679 --> 00:04:34.479
Tessla reports the package waves machinery taxes and inventory taxes for the first ten years.

00:04:35.059 --> 00:04:39.919
Tessla would still pay property taxes on structures, and the deal extends another five years

00:04:39.919 --> 00:04:41.839
if employment exceeds current targets.

00:04:42.459 --> 00:04:44.919
The race for the plant has narrowed to two locations,

00:04:45.239 --> 00:04:49.419
and Lamar consolidated independent school district has already added its own incentives.

00:04:50.259 --> 00:04:53.159
A Tesla site selection advisor told the Houston Chronicle

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:57.479
the final decision sits between one Texas site and one out-of-state option.

00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:01.379
The county director of economic development confirmed the extended

00:05:01.379 --> 00:05:06.843
abatement terms. Former Tesla engineers raised $23 million in Sydney to

00:05:06.843 --> 00:05:10.403
develop batteries for space applications, the Australian reports.

00:05:11.003 --> 00:05:14.743
The funding targets the growing space battery race, and the round was

00:05:14.743 --> 00:05:18.923
announced on October 27. The engineers left Tesla to focus on

00:05:18.923 --> 00:05:21.623
specialized cells for orbital and deep space use.

00:05:22.343 --> 00:05:25.703
Sydney investors backed the effort after reviewing early prototypes.

00:05:25.703 --> 00:05:31.638
The capital will support scaling production of radiation-hardened packs. Tesla designed

00:05:31.638 --> 00:05:37.118
the CyberCab battery pack to support cheaper lithium-iron phosphate or LFP chemistry in

00:05:37.118 --> 00:05:44.298
the future. Inside EVs reports the current 88s-6p pack uses 4680 cells in a steel enclosure.

00:05:44.878 --> 00:05:50.338
Each module is potted separately for individual replacement. Wireless battery management boards

00:05:50.338 --> 00:05:55.838
replaced traditional wiring harnesses. New contactors eliminated the need for a pyrophuse.

00:05:56.398 --> 00:06:01.498
The pack received an A- internal grade compared with lower scores for earlier structural packs.

00:06:02.533 --> 00:06:07.593
Robotics experts shared their assessments of Tesla's Optimus robot with IEEE spectrum.

00:06:07.993 --> 00:06:13.073
The discussion covered mechanical design, control systems, and potential deployment timelines.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:18.373
Experts noted both strengths in cost-focused engineering and remaining challenges in

00:06:18.373 --> 00:06:24.136
dexterity and reliability. A shareholder letter backing a Tesla SpaceX merger reached

00:06:24.136 --> 00:06:32.296
the board with 9,697 signers. Tesla Roddy reports, those signers hold 25.7 million shares

00:06:32.296 --> 00:06:39.396
representing roughly $10 billion. 76% of signers own both stocks. Elon stated any deal

00:06:39.396 --> 00:06:46.092
requires 50% of all Tesla shares. The petition was submitted in just over two days. Robert

00:06:46.092 --> 00:06:50.812
Reich called on Democrats to prepare groundwork for nationalizing SpaceX and Starlink.

00:06:51.572 --> 00:06:53.192
Elon Musk replied to the statement.

00:06:53.772 --> 00:06:57.392
The exchange followed Reich's public comments on potential policy steps.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:03.690
Retail CyberCab sales came up again when T.S. Alaming recalled Elon saying Tesla will eventually

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:07.370
let customers buy them and ask for clarification on the model.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:11.850
The post referenced an earlier statement about owner-operated robotaxies.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:17.360
Honor-operated cybercab still need a plant that can actually print them, and the assembly

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.260
method is what changes the economics.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:24.720
The cybercab splits into front, rear, side, and center modules that are built and tested

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:25.320
in parallel.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.460
Those modules meet at just 25 stations.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:32.360
That layout uses roughly half the floor space of a model Y line.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:35.360
Automation reaches 78% overall.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:38.340
The framing line is already at 100%.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:43.100
The result is a line that can already exceed current deployment rates without running every day.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:45.820
Engineers remove the paint shop entirely.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.320
They coat only the side modules inside the molding machine.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:55.660
That reversal moves the bottleneck from manufacturing to regulatory approval and city-by-city service agreements.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.340
When the factory can produce thousands of units per week in half the usual space,

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:06.560
expansion depends on how quickly new markets can absorb vehicles rather than how quickly the plant can be enlarged.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:15.340
Deleting the paint shop and coding only the side modules inside the molding machine further cuts capital and operating costs that would otherwise scale with volume.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:22.680
Lars Moravie noted during the Munro tour that the line does not run every day because output already outpaces deployments.

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:30.720
The same modular logic means future capacity additions need less incremental floor space and fewer stations than a conventional car plant.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:37.060
The 500,000-mile durability target built into the CyberCab supports high utilization economics

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.120
once those regulatory gates open.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:43.700
Capital intensity per additional vehicle falls once the first lines are running.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:49.360
That changes the cash flow profile of a Robotaxi network relative to earlier vehicle programs

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.880
that were stuck in production hell.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:56.300
Those choices lower the marginal cost of each extra unit once the initial lines are qualified.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:01.794
Before we go, Tesla's solar plant choice between Fort Bend County and the out-of-state

00:09:01.794 --> 00:09:04.394
option is still sitting with the site selection team.

00:09:04.814 --> 00:09:06.354
That's your Tesla news for today.

